@title Lesson walk: emc-on-the-plate (every step, Do it for me or Next)
@area Learn
# Starts the lesson from the palette and plays each step as a learner would: a reading step with Next, the chip steps by really clicking the chip (Do it for me only skips a click that is a control press, so it would leave the layer off). A picture and a layout check after each step.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text interference on the plate
wait 6
click_text "Interference on the plate: bonding and shield ends"
wait 40
shot 01-open-cabinet
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 02-emc-on
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 03-read-picture
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 04-bonding
check_layout
click_text "Bonding"
wait 30
shot 04b-bonding-on
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 06-shields
check_layout
click_text "Shields"
wait 30
shot 06b-shields-on-fix-it-step
check_layout
# Hot-spot markers off for one picture, so every ring and its kind is clear; the legend and the rings at full size are in scenarios 165 and 166.
click_text "Hot spots" Button
wait 20
shot 06c-shield-rings-clear
check_layout
click_text "Hot spots" Button
wait 10
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 08-leave
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot end
check_layout
